    "runs_where_an_ADMITTED_partner_carried_a_dead_edge": 78,
    "why_THAT_is_worse": "With no admissible partner the neighbour term drops out and the sensor is scored on physics, temporal and statistical checks alone, all of which read healthy. Measured on combination 0: from t=49.6 s the restricted trust climbs from 0.65 to 0.987 while the core stays pinned at 0.65. A sensor nothing is in a position to vouch for then reports HIGH trust -- the opposite error, and the exact state the corroboration guard exists to refuse to judge.",
    "why_that_matters": "Partner-level standing and edge-level agreement are different facts, and the restriction only filters on the first. Traced on combination 0 at t=40.0 s: motor_esc sat at 0.65000 with three incident edges all at consistency 0.0000, and the only ADMITTED partner was imu0 at trust 0.8528 against its att_caution standing of 0.82. imu0's bias drift breaks the accel/motor-current relation while imu0's own trust -- held up by its other edges and its physics checks -- stays above threshold. Restricting to partners in good standing therefore cannot clean the value: the contamination arrives through an admitted edge."
  },
